You sense the presence of spoilers. -more-

If the Murky hand blessed your sword, but didn't give you Excalibur,
then the only explanation I can think of is that Excalibur already
existed somewhere else in the dungeon.  If the Murky hand never
touched your sword, perhaps it was cursed.  (I think that has an
adverse effect on your chance of being given Excalibur.)  Or maybe you
just were having bad luck.  Incidentally, receiving Excalibur should
not be equated with being named the Hand of Elbereth.  The latter can
only be gained through #prayer and only by a (lucky) Lawful character.

>Also, what is a wand of undead turning good for?   I've never been
>able to get any percievable effect from one.

It repells undead or demons of equal or lesser level than yourself.
Ghosts are immune, though.  It will also restore any corpse to life.
I use them primarily for their amusement value, slaying a human
zombie or mummy and then resurrecting them and #chatting with them...
or killing them again.  ;)

